              <div class="tour-itinerary">
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
                  
                  <!-- STAGE 1 -->
                  <details class="premium-itinerary-item" open>
                    <summary class="premium-itinerary-summary">
                      <div class="itinerary-toggle-icon"></div>
                      <span>08:00 AM — Pickup at 195 De Tham, Homemade Bánh Mì & Lacquerware Stop</span>
                    </summary>
                    <div class="premium-itinerary-content custom-blog-prose max-w-none">
                      <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-md mb-6 border border-slate-200">
                        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 mb-2">Stage Highlights:</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-700 m-0 space-y-1">
                          <li>Pickup at 195 De Tham Street, District 1 in a private 7-seater van</li>
                          <li>Freshly made crispy Bánh Mì prepared by The Rice Travel Group's kitchen team</li>
                          <li>Visit Dai Viet Cu Chi Lacquerware Workshop & see master artisans at work</li>
                          <li>First set of candid travel photos captured by your dedicated photographer</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>08:00 AM — Guest Pickup at 195 De Tham Street, District 1:</strong> Your private air-conditioned 7-seater vehicle departs from central Saigon. Settle into your spacious seat and enjoy freshly baked Vietnamese bánh mì prepared by The Rice Travel Group's kitchen team throughout the 60–70 minute scenic drive to the northwestern outskirts.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>09:15 AM — Stop at Dai Viet Cu Chi Lacquerware Workshop:</strong> Before stepping into the historic combat zone, take a gentle pause at a traditional lacquerware workshop. Watch skilled craftsmen painstakingly create mother-of-pearl lacquer paintings, hand-embroidered art, and gemstone jewelry — a relaxing cultural introduction that eases your mind into the soul of Cu Chi.</p>
                    </div>
                  </details>

                  <!-- STAGE 2 -->
                  <details class="premium-itinerary-item">
                    <summary class="premium-itinerary-summary">
                      <div class="itinerary-toggle-icon"></div>
                      <span>10:00 AM — Documentary Screening & Ben Dinh Historical Tunnel Exploration</span>
                    </summary>
                    <div class="premium-itinerary-content custom-blog-prose max-w-none">
                      <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-md mb-6 border border-slate-200">
                        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 mb-2">Stage Highlights:</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-700 m-0 space-y-1">
                          <li>Watch a rare historical documentary about the resistance life of Cu Chi</li>
                          <li>Discover skillfully camouflaged secret trapdoors & decoy water wells</li>
                          <li>Explore the underground conference hall & see intact wrecked tank in the forest</li>
                          <li>Insightful, unhurried storytelling from your dedicated English-speaking guide</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>10:00 AM — Historical Documentary Screening:</strong> Begin your exploration with an authentic documentary film depicting the arduous daily life, defense strategies, and unbreakable spirit of the Cu Chi guerrilla forces — an essential historical foundation that rushed large-group tours frequently overlook.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>10:30 AM — Explore the Ben Dinh Tunnel Area:</strong> Walk beneath the shaded primeval forest to uncover ingeniously camouflaged secret wooden trapdoors (measuring barely 30x40 cm), decoy water wells, subterranean meeting halls, and an intact wrecked American M41 tank preserved amid the trees.</p>
                    </div>
                  </details>

                  <!-- STAGE 3 -->
                  <details class="premium-itinerary-item">
                    <summary class="premium-itinerary-summary">
                      <div class="itinerary-toggle-icon"></div>
                      <span>11:15 AM — Ben Duoc Tunnel Crawling & Underground Weapon Workshop</span>
                    </summary>
                    <div class="premium-itinerary-content custom-blog-prose max-w-none">
                      <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-md mb-6 border border-slate-200">
                        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 mb-2">Stage Highlights:</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-700 m-0 space-y-1">
                          <li>Firsthand tunnel crawling experience through multi-level underground systems</li>
                          <li>See termite-mound-simulated ventilation shafts & homemade booby traps</li>
                          <li>Visit the battlefield scrap metal weapon workshop beneath the ground</li>
                          <li>Optional sport shooting with real rifles (AK-47, M16) at the firing range</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>11:15 AM — Tunnel Crawling & Defense Systems:</strong> Head into the Ben Duoc tunnel sector for a safe, firsthand experience crawling through preserved underground sections. Observe the multi-tiered defensive layouts, hidden ventilation shafts designed like termite mounds, and displays of rudimentary yet effective bamboo and iron booby traps.</p>

                      <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 my-4 rounded-r-md">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2v-3a1 1 0 00-1-1H9z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                          </svg>
                          Experience Note & Photography
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-amber-900 text-base m-0">Crawling through the tunnels is completely optional. For those who prefer to stroll above ground under the cool forest shade, your dedicated photographer will capture stunning portrait shots with authentic vintage war relics.</p>
                      </div>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>12:00 PM — Weapon Workshop & Sport Shooting Range:</strong> Visit the underground workshop where unexploded battlefield ordnance was meticulously refashioned into specialized defense weapons. Guests may then try target shooting with AK-47 or M16 rifles at the national defense sports range (optional personal expense).</p>
                    </div>
                  </details>

                  <!-- STAGE 4 -->
                  <details class="premium-itinerary-item">
                    <summary class="premium-itinerary-summary">
                      <div class="itinerary-toggle-icon"></div>
                      <span>12:30 PM — Boiled Resistance Cassava & Scenic Return to Saigon</span>
                    </summary>
                    <div class="premium-itinerary-content custom-blog-prose max-w-none">
                      <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-md mb-6 border border-slate-200">
                        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 mb-2">Stage Highlights:</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-700 m-0 space-y-1">
                          <li>Savor hot boiled cassava dipped in savory peanut-sesame salt</li>
                          <li>Sip steaming jasmine tea in a peaceful open-air bamboo pavilion</li>
                          <li>Smooth return drive in your private 7-seater air-conditioned van</li>
                          <li>Full edited high-resolution photo collection delivered shortly after</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>12:30 PM — Savor Boiled Cassava with Peanut-Sesame Salt:</strong> Gather around a rustic bamboo pavilion under the Cu Chi forest canopy to savor the exact staple sustenance that kept fighters alive during the war: warm, soft boiled cassava dipped in crushed peanut-sesame salt, paired with a cup of hot jasmine tea. Simple, tranquil, and deeply memorable.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>01:00 PM — 02:00 PM — Return Transfer to Central Saigon:</strong> Board your private van for the relaxing return trip back to Ho Chi Minh City, arriving at 195 De Tham Street around 02:00 PM – 02:30 PM. Your guide and photographer bid you a warm farewell, sending over the complete high-resolution photo album right to your device!</p>
                    </div>
                  </details>

                </div>
              </div>
              
              <p style="font-style:italic;color:#64748b;font-size:1.0rem;margin-top:16px;padding:0 12px;">
                Note: The order of attractions may be flexibly tailored according to traffic conditions and guest preferences while ensuring 100% of signature experiences are delivered in full.
              </p>
